sparky-stereo-browser (@DEBVERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 360 videos and WebXR sessions work again when the browser is routed to a
    GPU that is not the one Stereo KWin renders on (+stereo3d10 drew a 360
    video twice in one view and VR ended the browser): a WebGL canvas keeps
    its layer and its stereo declaration, and the layer is copied to shared
    memory for the compositor. The picture's format and modifier are looked up
    in the tranches of the compositor's main device only.
  * Side by Side, Top and Bottom and Swap Eyes from the application menu act on
    the YouTube player's video (checked on a plain side by side video on both
    routes).

